      <li>Bottom Scrubber — Landsat & Sentinel-2 Satellite Timeline</li>
      <li>Right Rail — Key Telemetry Gauges & Live Ops Alerts</li>
      <li>Deep Dive Modal — Ward Drill-Down & Physics Attribution</li>
      <li>Overlay — AI Physics Optimization Scanner</li>
    </ul>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Step-by-Step 4-Minute Video Recording Script & Storyboard</strong></li>
  <li><strong>Key Differentiators & Judge Q&A Cheat Sheet</strong></li>
</ol>

<hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; margin: 25px 0;">

<h2>1. Executive App Summary & Value Proposition</h2>
<p><strong>UrbanIQ</strong> is an operational Decision Support System (DSS) engineered to combat the <strong>Urban Heat Island (UHI) effect</strong> across Pune, Maharashtra. Unlike traditional static heatmaps that merely display past temperature spikes, UrbanIQ provides a <strong>physics-informed, prescriptive decision matrix</strong>. It integrates:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Satellite Thermal Telemetry:</strong> Real Land Surface Temperature (LST), Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (NDVI), and Normalized Difference Built-Up Index (NDBI).</li>
  <li><strong>Administrative Voronoi Tessellation:</strong> 50 mutually exclusive, non-overlapping Pune municipal wards (from Hadapsar and Swargate to Bavdhan and Hinjawadi).</li>
  <li><strong>Physics-Informed Machine Learning (HistGradientBoosting / PINN):</strong> Real-time inference of temperature deltas when urban interventions (trees, cool roofs, reflective pavements) are applied.</li>
  <li><strong>Return on Investment (ROI) Optimization:</strong> Ranks interventions by cost efficiency (₹ Lakhs spent per °C averted) to assist municipal administrators under real budget caps.</li>
</ul>

<hr style="border: none; border-top: 1px solid #e2e8f0; margin: 25px 0;">

<h2>2. Complete Button & Interaction Catalog</h2>

<h3>A. Top Navigation & Header Controls</h3>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 25%;">Control / Button</th>
    <th style="width: 35%;">Visual & Technical Action</th>
    <th style="width: 40%;">What Happens on Screen / What to Demonstrate</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Toggle Control Panel (Sliders Icon)</strong></td>
    <td>Collapses or expands the Left Rail sidebar.</td>
    <td>Expands map visibility to 100% full-screen canvas when collapsed, then reopens smoothly. Great for showcasing wide map view.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>URBANIQ Brand Icon with Ping Badge</strong></td>
    <td>Displays satellite telemetry operational status with pulsing green radar ping.</td>
    <td>Reassures municipal stakeholders that the system is connected to live operational satellite passes.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>City Jurisdiction Selector ("Pune LIVE AI")</strong></td>
    <td>Opens a dropdown modal showing multi-city hackathon architecture (Pune active, others locked).</td>
    <td><strong>Click it!</strong> Shows that Pune is the primary active jurisdiction with 50 live AI wards, while other cities are architected for seamless multi-city expansion upon config ingestion.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Ward Autocomplete Search Box</strong></td>
    <td>Real-time live filter across all 50 Pune wards by name, ID (e.g., W-100), or zone.</td>
    <td><strong>Type "Hadapsar" or "Kothrud"</strong>. Instant dropdown shows temperature anomaly (+5.4°C) and canopy index. Clicking a result automatically flies to that ward and opens its detailed action brief.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Sensor Indicator ("SENSOR: Landsat-9 / Sentinel-2")</strong></td>
    <td>Displays current active satellite telemetry sensor and AI sync verification badge.</td>
    <td>Validates scientific rigor. Shows telemetry feed synchronicity.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Home Button</strong></td>
    <td>Navigates back to the Hero Landing Page.</td>
    <td>Allows smooth navigation between high-level policy landing overview and mission control map.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h3>B. Left Rail — Interactive Map Tools (Section 1)</h3>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 25%;">Tool Button</th>
    <th style="width: 35%;">Interaction Mechanism</th>
    <th style="width: 40%;">What Happens on Screen</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Point Select</strong></td>
    <td>Default mode. Clicking any ward selects or deselects it.</td>
    <td>Selected ward illuminates with a <strong>vibrant cyan border (3px) and translucent cyan highlight</strong>. Multi-select is fully supported! Top right counter updates to "X SELECTED".</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Lasso Tool</strong></td>
    <td>Click and drag freeform path across the map.</td>
    <td>Draws an animated glowing purple selection line on canvas. When released, Turf.js spatial intersection automatically selects all wards trapped inside the lasso loop!</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Plant Tree</strong></td>
    <td>Click anywhere on the map.</td>
    <td>Drops an emerald green tree pin on that exact coordinate. Automatically calculates local microclimate cooling contribution and adds to the scenario plan!</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Green Area (Polygon Tool)</strong></td>
    <td>Click 3 or more points, then double-click to close polygon.</td>
    <td>Fills an area with green canopy shading. Turf.js polygon overlay automatically increases vegetation delta (+0.15 NDVI) for any ward intersecting the boundary.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Clear Marks (Trash Icon)</strong></td>
    <td>Clears all selected wards, drawn tree pins, and user-drawn green polygons in one click.</td>
    <td>Instantly resets canvas selections and restores baseline municipal boundaries.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>GeoJSON Export (Download Icon)</strong></td>
    <td>Active whenever trees or green areas are drawn. Triggers browser file download.</td>
    <td>Generates a standardized <code>urban_heat_mitigation_plan.geojson</code> file for GIS technicians (QGIS/ArcGIS ready).</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h3>C. Left Rail — Satellite Telemetry GIS Layers (Section 2)</h3>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 25%;">GIS Layer Toggle</th>
    <th style="width: 35%;">Scientific Principle</th>
    <th style="width: 40%;">Visual Effect on Map</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>LST Surface Heat Layer</strong></td>
    <td>Thermal Infrared Satellite Telemetry (Landsat TIRS band).</td>
    <td>Renders all 50 Pune wards in calibrated thermal colors: <strong>Green (&lt;33°C) → Lime (34°C) → Yellow (35.5°C) → Orange (36.5°C) → Crimson Red (&gt;37.8°C)</strong>. Semitransparent so roads and geography stay visible!</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>NDVI Tree Canopy Density</strong></td>
    <td>Normalized Difference Vegetation Index (Sentinel-2 NIR/Red bands).</td>
    <td>Toggles vegetation canopy grading from barren brown/urban concrete (0.08) to dense forest green (0.38+). Shows inverse correlation with heat.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Physics Heat Drivers</strong></td>
    <td>Sensible heat flux and radiative albedo deficit attribution.</td>
    <td>Renders orange-red driver attribution circles at ward centroids sized and colored by thermal anomaly severity.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Vulnerable Population</strong></td>
    <td>Census demographics & elderly/slum dweller heat vulnerability index.</td>
    <td>Renders purple overlay circles scaled by vulnerable population count. Immediately identifies vulnerable slum and high-density zones.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>DISCOM Substation Stress</strong></td>
    <td>Grid cooling load telemetry (MW demand from AC & cooling units).</td>
    <td>Overlays electrical grid circles from yellow (50 MW) to flashing red (110 MW). Highlights transformer overload risk areas during heatwaves.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h3>D. Left Rail — Cooling Scenario Simulator (Section 3)</h3>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 25%;">Control</th>
    <th style="width: 35%;">Parameter Adjustment</th>
    <th style="width: 40%;">Dynamic System Response</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Tree Canopy Target Slider (0% to 50%)</strong></td>
    <td>Simulates Miyawaki urban afforestation and roadside shade trees.</td>
    <td>Dragging the slider instantly recalculates the <strong>Projected Impact Preview</strong> (-X.XX°C reduction) and updates the dynamic resilience gauge in real time!</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Cool Roof Coating Slider (0% to 100%)</strong></td>
    <td>Simulates high-albedo reflective rooftop coating (solar reflectance index &gt; 80).</td>
    <td>Reduces sensible heat absorption across industrial and slum tin roofs. Live calculation updates marginal cooling per ₹10 Lakhs.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Reflective Pavement Slider (0% to 50%)</strong></td>
    <td>Simulates permeable, reflective street and parking surfaces.</td>
    <td>Contributes additional thermal cooling flux to the municipal model.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Budget Allocation Input (₹ Lakhs)</strong></td>
    <td>Sets the municipal budget ceiling for the intervention plan.</td>
    <td>Automatically formats into Lakhs and Crores (e.g., ₹2.50 Cr). Modulates the budget constraint factor in the ML model.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Live Calculation Preview Card</strong></td>
    <td>Real-time client-side physics formula preview.</td>
    <td>Shows live predicted temp reduction (e.g. <code>-2.36°C</code>) and cost-efficiency (e.g. <code>0.094°C / ₹10L</code>).</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>"Run Cooling Optimiser" Button</strong></td>
    <td>Launches the multi-objective Pareto optimization scanner.</td>
    <td><strong>Triggers the full-screen scanning overlay!</strong> If specific wards are selected, optimizes strictly for those wards; otherwise optimizes city-wide.</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h3>E. Center Stage — MapLibre Interactive Map Canvas</h3>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 25%;">Map Element</th>
