<h3>H. Deep-Dive Modal — Ward Detail & Municipal Action Brief</h3>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 25%;">Modal Section</th>
    <th style="width: 35%;">Information Presented</th>
    <th style="width: 40%;">Actionable Municipal Value</th>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Header & Severity Tag</strong></td>
    <td>Zone Name, ID, Municipal Zone, and Risk Tag (CRITICAL / HIGH RISK).</td>
    <td>Instant categorization for field response teams.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>4 Telemetry Header Cards</strong></td>
    <td>LST Anomaly (+5.2°C), Surface Temp (38.0°C), Canopy Index (0.09), and Vulnerable Population (46%).</td>
    <td>Ground-truth data summary at a glance.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Physics-Informed Driver Attribution</strong></td>
    <td>Decomposes surface heat anomaly into:
      <ul>
        <li>Radiative Albedo Deficit (tin/asphalt)</li>
        <li>Sensible Heat Flux (low evapotranspiration)</li>
        <li>Anthropogenic Discharge (traffic/industry)</li>
      </ul>
    </td>
    <td>Includes model confidence intervals and governing physics formulas. Proves this is a physics-informed AI, not a black-box guess.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>Ranked Cooling Interventions (ROI per Rupee)</strong></td>
    <td>Ranked list of interventions with:
      <ul>
        <li>Estimated Cooling Impact (-°C)</li>
        <li>Implementation Cost (₹ Lakhs)</li>
        <li>Cost per degree averted (₹ L/°C)</li>
        <li>Co-benefits (biodiversity, energy savings)</li>
      </ul>
    </td>
    <td>Tells administrators exactly how to spend municipal funds for maximum thermal impact per rupee.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr>
    <td><strong>"Export Municipal Report" Button</strong></td>
    <td>Compiles the full ward telemetry, physics breakdown, and ranked ROI recommendations into a municipal action brief.</td>
    <td><strong>Click it in the demo!</strong> Immediately triggers a real file download (<code>URB-DSS-W-xxx-2026.txt</code>). Show the downloaded report on camera!</td>
  </tr>
</table>

<h3>I. Optimizing Overlay — AI Physics Scanner</h3>
<table>
  <tr>
    <th style="width: 25%;">Overlay Element</th>
