<h2>3. Step-by-Step 4-Minute Video Recording Script & Storyboard</h2>

<div class="script-box">
  <strong>PRO TIP FOR RECORDING:</strong> Record in 1080p or 4K. Use OBS Studio or Loom. Keep your mouse movements smooth and deliberate. Do not rush clicks.
</div>

<h3>[0:00 - 0:35] Scene 1: Introduction & The Core Problem</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Screen:</strong> Start on the <strong>Hero Landing Page</strong> (<code>http://localhost:5173/</code>).</li>
  <li><strong>Voiceover:</strong><br>
    <em>"Hello everyone. Extreme urban heatwaves are turning our cities into heat traps. In cities like Pune, asphalt, industrial metal rooftops, and vanishing tree canopy create severe microclimate hot zones that put vulnerable citizens and power grids at risk. Traditional satellite heatmaps tell city administrators that it is hot—but they do not tell them what to do about it, where to allocate limited budgets, or what ROI to expect.<br>
    This is <strong>UrbanIQ</strong>—a Physics-Informed Decision Support System for Municipal Heat Mitigation."</em>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Action:</strong> Click <strong>"Launch Mission Map"</strong> button. Smooth transition into the MapView.</li>
</ul>

<h3>[0:35 - 1:20] Scene 2: Interactive Pune Ward Heatmap & Spatial Segregation</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Screen:</strong> Mission Control Map with all 50 Pune wards.</li>
  <li><strong>Voiceover:</strong><br>
    <em>"Welcome to Mission Control. Here we see Pune partitioned into 50 contiguous, non-overlapping municipal wards generated via spatial Voronoi tessellation. Notice the calibrated thermal color coding: deep emerald green in forested buffers like Bavdhan and Pashan Lake at 33°C, progressing to lime green, yellow, orange, and critical crimson red in high-density corridors like Hadapsar MIDC and Swargate at over 38°C.<br>
    Our semi-transparent overlay preserves complete visibility of roads, rivers, and building footprints."</em>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Action:</strong>
    <ol>
      <li>Hover over a green ward (Bavdhan) to show tooltip: <code>33.0°C</code>, high NDVI.</li>
      <li>Hover over a red ward (Hadapsar MIDC): <code>38.4°C</code>, critical anomaly.</li>
      <li>Toggle between <strong>"Mission Dark"</strong> and <strong>"True Satellite"</strong> at the top right to show real rooftops and terrain.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>[1:20 - 2:05] Scene 3: Multi-Layer Satellite GIS Telemetry</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Screen:</strong> Left Rail Satellite Telemetry Layers.</li>
  <li><strong>Voiceover:</strong><br>
    <em>"UrbanIQ layers multimodal geospatial data to explain why hotspots occur. In the left panel, we can toggle our satellite GIS layers."</em>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Action:</strong>
    <ol>
      <li>Click <strong>"NDVI Tree Canopy Density"</strong> → Show how tree canopy directly inverses the heat map.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>"Physics Heat Drivers"</strong> → Red circles appear highlighting sensible heat flux and low albedo.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>"Vulnerable Population"</strong> → Purple demographic circles reveal exposed elderly and low-income populations.</li>
      <li>Click <strong>"DISCOM Substation Stress"</strong> → Yellow and red electrical grid circles highlight transformers under severe AC cooling load.</li>
      <li>Point out the dynamic badge: <code>"5 ACTIVE"</code> layers.</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>[2:05 - 2:50] Scene 4: Interactive Intervention Tools & Sliders</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Screen:</strong> Interactive Map Tools and Cooling Simulator Sliders.</li>
  <li><strong>Voiceover:</strong><br>
    <em>"Now, let us look at prescription and what-if simulation. Administrators can select specific target zones or draw direct spatial interventions."</em>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Action:</strong>
    <ol>
      <li>Click <strong>"Lasso Tool"</strong> → Draw a smooth circle around 2 or 3 central wards. They illuminate in bright cyan with white boundaries!</li>
      <li>Click <strong>"Plant Tree"</strong> → Drop 2 tree pins inside the selected zone.</li>
      <li>Move to the sliders: Drag <strong>Tree Canopy Target</strong> to <code>+25%</code>, and <strong>Cool Roof Coating</strong> to <code>50%</code>.</li>
      <li>Point to the <strong>Live Calculation Preview Card</strong>: watch the cooling drop by <code>-2.4°C</code>.</li>
      <li>Point to the <strong>Resilience Gauge</strong> on the right rail: show the live projected improvement (<code>+14 pts projected</code>).</li>
    </ol>
  </li>
</ul>

<h3>[2:50 - 3:30] Scene 5: AI Physics Cooling Optimizer</h3>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Screen:</strong> Running the Optimizer.</li>
  <li><strong>Voiceover:</strong><br>
    <em>"Next, we run our Physics-Informed Machine Learning Optimizer to solve the budget constraint problem."</em>
  </li>
  <li><strong>Action:</strong>
    <ol>
      <li>Click <strong>"Run Cooling Optimiser"</strong>.</li>
